### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The CDC estimated 61,200 flu deaths for the 2018–2019 season, not the claimed 75,000, and estimated 24,000–62,000 deaths for the 2019–2020 season ([Time](https://time.com/5610878/2018-2019-flu-season/), [ContagionLive](https://www.contagionlive.com/view/how-deadly-was-the-2019-2020-flu-season)). While COVID-19 mitigation measures correlated with reduced flu activity, laboratory-confirmed deaths and CDC estimates still numbered in the thousands, and reporting disruptions made direct comparisons incomplete ([USA Today](https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/factcheck/2020/04/30/fact-check-cdc-still-tracking-flu-deaths-2019-20-typical/4880048001/)). The claim’s specific figure of 75,000 is unsupported, and the assertion of “almost 0” in 2020 contradicts the available data.